[i]{Silas.name} sits by himself at the dining table, reading a book. His leg bounces nervously as you walk up to him.[/i]
[i]When you approach, he turns up from his book to look at you.[/i]
Silas (Default): "Oh hey. I was hoping that you'd stop by to talk a little bit."
Silas (Sad): "I'm going to go out to look for {FoShi.name} after the rain stops, and I just wanted to tell you again that I'm really sorry about making you kick him out."
- "We'll find him."
	Player: "We'll find him. Don't worry so much."
	Silas: "It's hard not to worry when we have no idea where he is."
- "It's not your fault."
	Player (Happy): "It's not your fault. I was the one who made the final call on it."
	Silas (Sad): "You know how I feel about this. It doesn't matter if you made the final call or not, I was the one who told you to."
- "Don't worry about it. It was justified."
	Player: "Don't worry about it. It was justified. His gang were the ones who destroyed your home."
	Silas: "You've seen it yourself, he's changed. That's why I'm going out to look for him."
- "You need to make up for it."
	Player (Angry): "You need to make up for doing that. Good thing you're going out to look for him."
	Silas (Angry): "If you're going to be like that, I'm not going to talk to you."
	set {Silas.silas_friendship} -= 5.0
	- "I'm sorry, I'm just stressed."
		Player (Sad): "I'm sorry, I'm just really stressed right now."
		Silas (Angry): "We all are. That's not an excuse to be a jerk."
		[i]{Silas.name} turns away from you and refuses to interact more.[/i]
		[end_timeline]
	- "I'm just telling the truth."
		Player (Default): "I'm just telling the truth."
		Silas: "Then we don't have anything else to talk about."
		[i]{Silas.name} turns away from you and refuses to interact more.[/i]
		[end_timeline]
	- "I didn't want to talk to you anyway."
		Player (Angry): "I didn't want to talk to you anyway."
		Silas (Angry): "Then why did you come over here in the first place?"
		[i]{Silas.name} turns away from you and refuses to interact more.[/i]
		[end_timeline]
[i]{Silas.name} fidgets with his hands for a little bit before speaking again.[/i]
Silas (Happy): "I also wanted to say that I'm thankful to you for providing shelter and food. I was getting a little low on supplies and I wasn't really sure where I would find more."
Silas (Default): "I was also wondering if you know a recipe for tater tot casserole? I've been wanting to have it for a while but can't recall any."
- "That's a midwest thing, right?" | [if {Silas.from} != "????"] [else="disable" alt_text="something"]
	Player (Happy): "That's a midwest thing, right? Oh yeah, you're from Wisconsin. Is it good?"
	Silas (Happy): "Yeah, it's really good! It doesn't even need a ton of ingredients either!"
	Player (Default): "I guess I'll have to try it out then sometime."
	Silas (Happy): "I'll hold you to it!"
	set {Silas.silas_friendship} += 5.0
- "Why that specifically? Sounds weird."
	Player (Default): "Why that specifically? Sounds weird. Is that like a regional dish or something?"
	Silas (Shock): "Yeah it is. Didn't I tell you I'm from {Silas.from}?"
- "Can't say that I do."
	Player (Default): "Can't say that I do. I've never heard of tater tot casserole."
	Silas (Happy): "Oh, you have to try it then! It's really good!"
[i]The rain outside sets a low background noise for the conversation as it drifts off. Neither of you have anything more to say to each other.[/i]
Silas (Happy): "Well, I'll let you get back to doing whatever you were doing then!"
[i]He turns back to the book he was reading, leaving you to go about your business.[/i]